{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1288308-converting-1e-npcs-to-2e","id":1288308,"title":"Converting 1e NPCs to 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-15T09:59:12-08:00","id":1288308,"title":"Converting 1e NPCs to 2e","content":"So I\u2019ve been trying to use some the stat blocks form the older books and it looks like the Gnosis and Arcanum limits may be a little different between editions. Like maybe Mages in 2e might have a little bit higher Gnosis than the did in 1e. Anyone really familiar with both editions have any thoughts or advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:03:01-08:00","id":1288330,"title":"","content":"I'd say threat it the same. I think 1e's arcana limits were in place to encourage certain kinds of behaviors that players usually don't have time to do or prepare for cuz like, how many mages would actually accumulate like 20+ dots before they were gnosis 5? So the arcana limits were simplified because it wasn't necessary, the arcana limits in 1e just never became relevant for most characters.<br /> <br /> The idea though is to encourage versatility and multiple arcana, I think, as opposed to powering up gnosis and 1 single arcana as much as possible. The prerequisites for Archmastery also did this, you need 3 arcana at adept level and mastery of a 4th to do it, so you need versatility.<br /> <br /> So my gut is that you don't need to change their stats too much or make them stronger, because they're already way stronger cuz of praxes, rotes, reach, and automatic potency/duration rules all make these npcs way more versatile and powerful than their 1e stats might suggest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:25:33-08:00","id":1288335,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the arcana limits are different. I've found a good few characters needed an extra gnosis dot to cover the arcana they have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T11:34:38-08:00","id":1288339,"title":"","content":"In general it seems like Gnosis is spread a bit more evenly this time? It seems like in 1e high Gnosis as for Archmages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:",